From: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] etnaviv/teflon: add HW_V83 NN and TP_ENGINE=0 fallback support

Support VeriSilicon VIP9000Nano-DI (0x9202, Allwinner A733) and other
HW_V83 NPU variants that expose:

- TP_ENGINE=0 (no hardware Tensor Processor): report tp_core_count=0
  instead of defaulting to 1, reject standalone TP ops (PAD/RELU/ABS/
  LOGISTIC) so TFLite runs them on CPU, and execute internal layout
  conversions (TRANSPOSE, DETRANSPOSE, RESHUFFLE) on CPU with proper
  GPU batch synchronization.
- NN_CMD_SUPPORT_SLICE=1: program in_image_y_stride and
  out_image_y_stride as channel-slice byte strides (x_size * y_size)
  rather than row counts.
- FP_INIMAGE_POST_SCALE=1: encode post_shift (including bit 7 in
  w15[30]) as the raw IEEE-754 biased float32 exponent alongside the
  23-bit mantissa in post_multiplier*.
- NN_TENSOR_ADD_FIELD_MOVE_TO_EXT_CMD=1: decline ADD/SUBTRACT on the
  NN engine until HW_V83 extended-command addition lowering is
  implemented.

